/**
 * Nose lean in radians for the current flight state — a smooth gravity
 * turn. The ship climbs vertically off the pad (0), pitches over while it
 * accelerests into its space cruising leg (toward PI/2 = flat, flying
 * along the orbit), then eases back to vertical (0) to come down retro-
 * first and land upright. The lean is eased each frame, so every change
 * of attitude is gradual rather than a snap.
 */
public float getFlightTilt() {
    return attitude;
}

/** Yaw (radians) the nose leans toward — follows the direction of travel. */
public float getHeading() {
    return heading;
}

